de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000139946","entrez_id":["57161"],"uniprot":["Q9HAT8"],"ncbi_summary":"Predicted to enable protein-macromolecule adaptor activity and ubiquitin protein ligase activity. Acts upstream of or within positive regulation of MAPK cascade and positive regulation of protein phosphorylation. Predicted to be located in membrane. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9HAT8","text":"E3 ubiquitin ligase catalyzing the covalent attachment of ubiquitin moieties onto substrate proteins (PubMed:17675297, PubMed:17997719, PubMed:38917796). Specifically recognizes and binds proteins phosphorylated on threonine residues (PubMed:19081057, PubMed:38917796). Involved in the TLR and IL-1 signaling pathways via interaction with the complex containing IRAK kinases and TRAF6 (PubMed:12860405, PubMed:17997719, PubMed:22669975). Mediates IL1B-induced IRAK1 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitination and possibly 'Lys-48'-linked ubiquitination (PubMed:12860405, PubMed:17997719). Acts as a negative regulator of cGAS-STING signaling: recognizes and binds phosphorylated STING1 and mediates 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitination of TBK1, inhibiting cGAS-STING signaling, while simultaneously enhancing the STING1-dependent NF-kappa-B axis (PubMed:38917796). May be important for LPS- and IL1B-induced MAP3K7-dependent, but not MAP3K3-dependent, NF-kappa-B activation (PubMed:12804775). Can activate the MAP (mitogen activated protein) kinase pathway leading to activation of ELK1 (PubMed:12804775)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}